{"id": "sllama0000", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are seven colors in a rainbow. They are red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, and violet.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0008", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The smallest continent is Australia.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0016", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The capital of Brazil is Brasília. It's located in the central part of the country and was designed as a modernist city when it was built in the 196 0s to serve as the new capital, replacing Rio de Janeiro.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0024", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Shema prayer consists of two main parts. The first part, which is the declaration of faith, has about 20 words in He brew. The second part, which includes a blessing and a reminder to love the Lord with all your heart, mind, soul, and strength, adds another few words. So altogether, it's roughly around 30 to 40 words depending on how you count them.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0032", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The largest city in Sc andinavia is Stock holm, Sweden. It' s not only the biggest city in the region but also serves as the capital of Sweden. Known for its stunning architecture, historic sites like the Old Town and modern design, it's a vibrant hub for culture, commerce, and innovation.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0040", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "That's a good question. I think the most ven omous animal in the world is probably the box jellyfish. It has many tentacles filled with thousands of tiny stinging cells called nematocysts, which can cause severe pain and even death if not treated quickly.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0048", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The smallest insect in the world is a fairy fly, specifically certain species from the family Mymaridae. Some of these tiny parasitic wasps can measure less than half a millimeter in length, making them incredibly small compared to most other insects.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0056", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Table tennis is also known as ping pong.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0064", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The founder of the Baha i Faith is Bah au'll ah. He established the faith in the 19th century and taught that all major religion s come from one divine source.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0072", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Portland is known for its craft beer scene. It has a really vibrant culture of small breweries and brew pubs that offer all kinds of unique beers.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0080", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for Fran cium is F r. It' s a very rare and highly radioactive element found in nature, usually only in trace amounts.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0088", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The famous painting, \" The Star ry Night,\" was painted by Vincent van Gogh. He created it in 1889 while he was staying at a mental health asylum in France. It' s one of his most recognizable works and is known for its swirling sky and vibrant colors.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0096", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The first African American to win an Olympic gold medal was Thomas H. Hall in the 1896 Olympics in Athens, Greece. He won the triple jump event.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0104", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The organ responsible for filter ing waste products from the blood is the kidney. They play a key role in removing extra water and waste, like urea and uric acid, to form urine, which helps keep the body balanced and healthy.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0112", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The bright object in the night sky that is not a star could be several things. It might be a planet like Ven us or Jupiter, which can appear very bright. Another possibility is an artificial satellite, such as the International Space Station, which reflects sunlight and gl ows brightly when it passes overhead. Sometimes it can also be a meteorite, though those are usually brief flashes. If you see something steady and bright for a while, it's likely a planet or a satellite.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 26, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0120", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Sauron appears in the book The Lord of the Rings by J.R.R. Tol kien. He's a powerful evil being who rules over Mordor and seeks to conquer Middle-earth with his dark powers.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0128", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The lion is known for its majestic mane.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0136", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "That would be the movie called King Kong. It's about a giant monkey that' s captured and brought to New York City.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0144", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Rice is the most consumed food in the world. It is a staple food for more than half of the global population, especially in Asia. People eat it with almost every meal, whether it' s plain or cooked with vegetables, meat, or other ingredients. Its versatility, low cost, and cultural significance make it a daily part of life for billions of people around the globe.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 21, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0152", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "As of 20 24, the most followed artist on Instagram is Cristiano Ron aldo. He has over 500 million followers, making him one of the most popular account s on the platform.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0160", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Erica Durance played Lois Lane on the TV show Smallville.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0168", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The medical term for the sensation of itching is pruritus. It can be caused by dry skin, all ergies, or underlying conditions like liver disease or kidney issues.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0176", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "That term is called adaptation. It' s the process by which an organism becomes better suited to its environment over time. For example, polar bear s have evolved thick fur and layer ed fat to stay warm in the Arctic.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0184", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The deepest part of the ocean is called the Mariana T rench. It's located in the Pacific O cean, near the island of Guam. Its depth reaches about 36, 000 feet, or roughly 11, 000 me ters. That makes it the lowest point on Earth below sea level.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0192", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The animal with the longest lifespan is the quino id turtle, which can live up to 15 0 years or more. It's a really long- lived creature!", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0200", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The first season of Survivor was won by Richard Hatch. He was the sole survivor on Borneo and took home the million dollar prize.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0208", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "In Sikh ism, there are 10 articles of faith known as the Ten Vows or the Das Vai ragya. These principles guide Sikh spiritual ity and ethical living. They include vow s such as not killing any creature, not stealing, being honest in speech and actions, and remaining devoted to God through constant prayer and meditation.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 23, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0216", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The largest lake in Asia is Lake Baik al. It's located in southern Siberia, Russia. It's not only the biggest lake by surface area but also holds the world record for depth. It goes down over 1,6 4 2 meters.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0224", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Adult humans typically have 32 teeth, including 8 incisors, 4 can ines, 8 premolars, and 12 molar s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0232", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are seven continent s in the world. They are Africa, Antarctica, Asia, Europe, North America, South America, and Australia.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0240", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Diverg ence series by Veronic a Roth consists of four books. They are Diver gence, Ins urgence, Al egiance, and finally, Ascendan ce. So there are four books in total.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0248", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The name of the treaty that ended World War I was the Treaty of Versailles.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
